paragraph_patches.before:
The instance labels restricted to $C$ define partitions $P,Q$. Using natural logarithms, their variation of information is $\mathrm{VI}=H(P\mid Q)+H(Q\mid P)$, and their joint entropy is $H=H(P,Q)$. Following established information-theoretic comparisons~\cite{vinh2010}, we examine
\begin{equation}
 Q_1=\frac{\mathrm{VI}}{\log |C|},\quad Q_2=\frac{\mathrm{VI}}{H},\quad D_k=A+wQ_k.
\end{equation}
We call $D_1$ FA-v1 and $D_2$ FA-v2. Their partition-only controls are $wQ_1$ and $wQ_2$, respectively. These are named analysis variants, not claims to new mathematical distances. Partition terms are zero for $|C|\leq1$ or zero joint entropy. Two empty foregrounds yield zero disagreement; exactly one empty foreground yields total disagreement one. Scores are averaged over the three member pairs before aggregation across bone units.

paragraph_patches.after:
The instance labels restricted to $C$ define partitions $P,Q$: each partition says which shared voxels belong to the same fragment. Using natural logarithms, variation of information is $\mathrm{VI}=H(P\mid Q)+H(Q\mid P)$, where conditional entropy measures the fragment information one prediction fails to determine about the other. Let $H=H(P,Q)$ denote joint entropy. Following established information-theoretic comparisons~\cite{vinh2010}, we examine
\begin{equation}
 Q_{\rm vox}=\frac{\mathrm{VI}}{\log |C|},\qquad
 Q_{\rm joint}=\frac{\mathrm{VI}}{H},
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
 D_{\rm vox}=A+wQ_{\rm vox},\qquad
 D_{\rm joint}=A+wQ_{\rm joint}.
\end{equation}
The subscripts identify normalization by voxel count or joint entropy. Each combined score adds presence disagreement to a weighted partition term; $wQ_{\rm vox}$ and $wQ_{\rm joint}$ are its partition-only controls. Increasing voxel count can enlarge $\log|C|$ even when the fragment proportions stay the same. Joint-entropy normalization instead depends on those proportions, making the denominator choice directly testable. These are analysis variants of established quantities, not proposed new mathematical distances. Partition terms are zero for $|C|\leq1$ or zero joint entropy. Two empty foregrounds yield zero disagreement; exactly one empty foreground yields total disagreement one. Scores are averaged over the three model pairs before aggregation across bone units.
